WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:04.032
Use Upgrade Advisor to identify evidence needed before an upgrade.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:08.640
Enter the cluster context and reviewed P E and optional P C connections.

00:00:09.003 --> 00:00:11.345
Establish verified certificate trust first.

00:00:11.598 --> 00:00:15.864
The advisor does not execute upgrades or certify a supported upgrade path.

00:00:16.291 --> 00:00:21.411
Verify T L S certificate is enabled separately for P E and P C inventory

00:00:21.496 --> 00:00:22.080
collection.

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.077
Administrators can use an explicitly scoped temporary exception where

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:26.866
authorized.

00:00:27.144 --> 00:00:31.282
It resets after collection, is audited, and is preserved as a qualification

00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:33.862
in saved inventory and assessment reports.

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:36.441
Review that qualification with the findings.

00:00:36.675 --> 00:00:40.899
An exception weakens identity assurance for that collection; it is not a

00:00:40.942 --> 00:00:43.478
trust repair or a general workflow setting.

00:00:43.837 --> 00:00:47.592
Other workflows, drift checks and recovery keep their own certificate

00:00:47.635 --> 00:00:48.246
policies.

00:00:48.702 --> 00:00:52.584
Collect fresh inventory and inspect the timestamp, returned fields and

00:00:52.627 --> 00:00:53.623
collection errors.

00:00:53.936 --> 00:00:59.226
P E cluster and host reads can supply A O S and homogeneous A H V versions.

00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:03.536
P C product-header detection is limited context, not an authenticated

00:01:03.664 --> 00:01:04.474
permission test.

00:01:04.645 --> 00:01:07.405
Other components can remain manual or unknown.

00:01:07.691 --> 00:01:10.692
Do not replace missing values with guessed versions.

00:01:11.062 --> 00:01:14.429
Enter the intended target versions and environment signals.

00:01:14.681 --> 00:01:19.631
Review release notes, compatibility, lifecycle prechecks and any dark-site

00:01:19.716 --> 00:01:22.425
bundle requirements using the actual vendor material.

00:01:22.788 --> 00:01:25.249
Mark evidence complete only when it was reviewed.

00:01:25.492 --> 00:01:29.204
Curated rule packs contribute explicit guardrails and sources.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:33.385
They are not an automatic scrape of every support article or private defect

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:33.840
record.

00:01:34.323 --> 00:01:38.163
Run the assessment and review each blocker, warning, review item and

00:01:38.206 --> 00:01:38.940
unknown.

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:43.129
Read the guidance, source and missing evidence rather than looking only at

00:01:43.172 --> 00:01:44.260
an overall score.

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.726
Assign the necessary follow-up and collect its real evidence.

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:52.365
A clear result remains limited to the reviewed inputs and rules; it does not

00:01:52.408 --> 00:01:56.014
replace actual lifecycle checks or authorize change execution.

00:01:56.486 --> 00:02:00.283
Save the reviewed assessment with its owner and context, then export the

00:02:00.326 --> 00:02:01.819
evidence bundle if required.

00:02:02.161 --> 00:02:04.998
The snapshot preserves the assessed inputs and findings.

00:02:05.275 --> 00:02:09.313
Collecting newer inventory later does not rewrite that saved assessment.

00:02:09.638 --> 00:02:13.264
Compare a new snapshot when conditions change and retain the relevant

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:17.188
version with the change record and final vendor precheck results.
